er british territory  i also spoke to lee chuk yan and this is  what he had to say on his way into court  in this day of reckoning  the political suppression is equally to  all  those who have take part in the protest  movement including  no matter where you are the peaceful no  knowledge or the braver  you are all caught under this political  suppression way  so they've been convicted if this group  gets sent to  prison where does this leave hong kong's  pro-democracy movement  well it certainly is a blow to the  movement uh nearly every  major voice or or of dissent or figure  of opposition is now either in exile  in jail already or on trial now more  than 2  400 people have been charged as part of  this crackdown  at the likes of jimmy ly the media  tycoon who i spoke about earlier he's  currently  in custody he's also facing six other  trials  one of those under the national security  law we also have league chucky and he's  facing  three different trials uh they're  separate charges but separate but  similar charges i should say  uh so certainly this particular  pro-democracy movement uh it's a blow to  it  uh the the movement says that this is  the national security law  is beijing's attempt to crack down or  silence the opposition  in hong kong another veteran activist i  spoke to on the way into court she said  the movement will simply have to find  other ways of showing the opposition to  china  and fighting for the freedoms in hong  kong that were promised at the 1997  agreement  al jazeera sarah clark reporting live  from hong kong sarah many thanks
 

